  "scenes": [
    {
      "text": "Right now, as the fall storms roll back into Washington State, America's most dangerous volcano looks calm.",
      "emphasis": "AMERICA'S MOST DANGEROUS VOLCANO",
      "lowerThird": {
        "title": "Washington State",
        "subtitle": "Fall 2026"
      },
      "broll": [
        "storm clouds mountain timelapse",
        "mount rainier clouds aerial"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Peaceful. Picture *perfect*.",
      "broll": [
        "mount rainier lake reflection",
        "archive:Mount Rainier Reflection Lake"
      ],
      "transition": "zoom"
    },
    {
      "text": "But a little over a year ago, deep beneath its icy summit, that mountain started *shaking* like it never had before.",
      "look": "dramatic",
      "badge": "2025",
      "broll": [
        "archive:Mount Rainier summit crater glacier",
        "archive:seismograph recording"
      ],
      "transition": "glitch",
      "fx": [
        "shake"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Not once. Not a few times. Over and over and over again.",
      "fx": [
        "punch"
      ],
      "broll": [
        "archive:seismogram earthquake",
        "glacier crevasse aerial"
      ],
      "transition": "whip"
    },
    {
      "text": "At its peak, instruments were catching earthquakes at a pace of roughly *40* every single hour.",
      "broll": [
        "archive:seismogram earthquake swarm",
        "archive:Cascades Volcano Observatory"
      ],
      "transition": "flash"
    },
    {
      "text": "By the time it was finally over, more than *1,350* earthquakes had been pinned down beneath the summit, with thousands more too small to even locate.",
      "emphasis": "1,350 EARTHQUAKES",
      "broll": [
        "archive:Mount Rainier summit aerial",
        "glacier ice mountain drone"
      ],
      "transition": "zoom"
    },
    {
      "text": "It was the biggest earthquake swarm ever recorded at this mountain.",
      "broll": [
        "archive:Mount Rainier from Paradise",
        "snow mountain drone"
      ],
      "transition": "whip"
    },
    {
      "text": "And according to the scientists who watch it, the hidden process that caused all that shaking may *still* be going on right now, just too quietly for their instruments to pick up.",
      "fx": [
        "reveal"
      ],
      "look": "night",
      "broll": [
        "volcano steam fumarole",
        "mount rainier night stars"
      ],
      "transition": "dip"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mountain is *Mount Rainier*.",
      "lowerThird": {
        "title": "Mount Rainier",
        "subtitle": "14,410 ft | Pierce County, WA"
      },
      "broll": [
        "archive:Mount Rainier"
      ],
      "transition": "flash"
    },
    {
      "text": "The same snowy peak that floats over the Seattle skyline on a clear day.",
      "broll": [
        "seattle skyline mount rainier",
        "seattle space needle"
      ],
      "transition": "zoom"
    },
    {
      "text": "The same peak printed on license plates and postcards and coffee cups.",
      "broll": [
        "archive:Mount Rainier postcard",
        "coffee cup cafe"
      ],
      "transition": "whip"
    }
  ],
